  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "Jeffrey Drum, a researcher, looks at a 2020 study that used a kind of satellite radar imaging to see inside the Great Pyramid of Giza in Egypt. He says that in the scan he does not see a clear signature for the King's Chamber, one of the best-known rooms inside the pyramid. That matters because it raises the question of how well the method sees what is really there."
